Harbor: Direct2D has the 3D transform, atlas and tile effects (#93).

Excel creates them; creating one failed with D2DERR_EFFECT_IS_NOT_REGISTERED. They are declared like the other
built-in effects here: the properties exist and can be set, and there is no processing of their own behind them.
Seen from Excel in a start with a workbook open: these three, and scale, colour matrix and flood, which exist.
Which of 0025 to 0028 Excel's blank window was down to was not separated for this one; without 0027 alone the
window stays blank.

Test: WindowsTests/d2d/run.sh.

